**🔴 Security: XSS vulnerability in dynamic field HTML generation**

**File:** `app/javascript/controllers/dynamic_fields_controller.js:24`

The addField() method directly inserts HTML using template literals without sanitizing user input values. When loading existing data, if the specification_pdp JSON contains malicious scripts, they will be rendered as executable HTML.

**Current Code:**
```javascript
const fieldHtml = `
  <div class="flex items-center space-x-2 mb-2" data-field-index="${this.fieldCount}">
    <input type="text" placeholder="Group"
```

**Suggested Fix:**
```javascript
// Add this method:
escapeHtml(text) {
  const div = document.createElement('div');
  div.textContent = text;
  return div.innerHTML;
}

// Use it in template:
value="${this.escapeHtml(groupValue || '')}"
```

**Recommendation:** CRITICAL: Add XSS protection by implementing escapeHtml() and sanitizing all user values before inserting into DOM.

---
