**🟡 Warning: Dynamic fields won't load existing data on edit**

**File:** `app/javascript/controllers/dynamic_fields_controller.js:12`

The initializeExistingFields() method doesn't parse the hidden field's value. When editing products with existing specification_pdp, fields will be empty.

**Suggested Implementation:**
```javascript
initializeExistingFields() {
  const hiddenField = document.querySelector('[name="product[specification_pdp]"]')
  if (hiddenField && hiddenField.value) {
    try {
      const data = JSON.parse(hiddenField.value)
      this.loadExistingData(data)
    } catch (e) {
      console.error('Failed to parse specification_pdp:', e)
    }
  }

  if (this.fieldCount === 0) {
    this.addField()
  }
}

loadExistingData(groupedData) {
  Object.entries(groupedData).forEach(([group, specs]) => {
    specs.forEach(spec => {
      this.addFieldWithData(group, spec.name, spec.value)
    })
  })
}
```

